  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 234 AM CDT Wed Sep 23 2026\n\nLowered highs for today as NBM looks to be too warm again given the \nexpected cloud cover today and yesterday's outcome. The upper low \ndrifts southeast today and cloud cover should diminish accordingly \nlater on. Upper ridging builds over the Midwest Thursday and Friday. \nThere is the potential for a shortwave to squash the ridge \ntemporarily this weekend which could lead to some precip chances on \nSunday. Confidence isn't high at this time though due to model \ndiscrepancies. NBM is mainly dry at this point except for a small \narea in SEMO with 20% PoPs on Sunday. \n\nThe next main system looks to come through around mid-week with a \nlongwave trof aloft. Timing is low confidence at this point. NBM \nbrings in widespread PoPs from the west by Tuesday evening and they \nramp up into Wednesday. All of this is still a ways out and subject \nto change of course.",
